Spatial map save: don't replace the map with a 0-byte file on a full disk

Qt 5.15's QSaveFile only records errors from write(), not from the buffered
flush inside commit(). On a full disk a small file therefore "commits"
successfully as 0 bytes and replaces the real map (2026-09-17 incident: all
per-activity spatial-desktop-nav-*.json maps wiped). Flush and verify
explicitly, and cancel the write so the previous file survives.

Applied and deployed in ~/ws/kwin-dev/kwin/src/virtualdesktops.cpp on
2026-09-17; still needs porting into the rig (mayor/rig/src/virtualdesktops.cpp).
Verified the flush()/cancelWriting() behaviour with a Qt 5.15.3 test program on
a full tmpfs: old file kept, whereas plain write()+commit() left 0 bytes.

--- a/src/virtualdesktops.cpp
+++ b/src/virtualdesktops.cpp
@@ void VirtualDesktopSpatialMap::saveJson(const QString &filePath, const QStringList &knownIds,
     QSaveFile file(filePath);
     if (!file.open(QIODevice::WriteOnly)) {
         qWarning() << "VirtualDesktopSpatialMap: cannot open" << filePath << "for writing";
         return;
     }
-    file.write(QJsonDocument(root).toJson());
+    // Qt 5.15's QSaveFile only records errors from write(), not from the buffered
+    // flush inside commit(): on a full disk a small file "commits" as 0 bytes and
+    // replaces the real map. Flush and verify explicitly so the old file survives.
+    const QByteArray data = QJsonDocument(root).toJson();
+    if (file.write(data) != data.size() || !file.flush() || file.size() != data.size()) {
+        qWarning() << "VirtualDesktopSpatialMap: write failed for" << filePath << "-"
+                   << file.errorString() << "- keeping previous file";
+        file.cancelWriting();
+        return;
+    }
     if (!file.commit()) {
         qWarning() << "VirtualDesktopSpatialMap: failed to commit" << filePath;
     }
